# Paths whose contents EXECUTE AS ROOT on a hypervisor, or decide what does.
#
# substrate is going public, so the set of people who can open a pull request is
# no longer the set of people who should have root on these machines. Requiring
# a code-owner review on these paths is what keeps those two sets apart.
#
# ⚠️ This file is ADVISORY until "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in
# branch protection for `main`. GitHub will show the reviewer request either
# way, which is exactly the kind of control that looks enforced and is not —
# so it is said here rather than assumed.

# Everything, by default.
*                               @bradpenney

# --- root-executing surface -------------------------------------------------
# Unit files: what systemd starts, as whom, with what privileges.
/systemd/                       @bradpenney
# Shell run by those units, most of it as root.
/*.sh                           @bradpenney
# The deployers: they compose the privileged installer itself.
/crates/substrate-core/src/updates.rs        @bradpenney
/crates/substrate-core/src/observability/    @bradpenney
/crates/substrate-core/src/cplb.rs           @bradpenney
/crates/substrate-core/src/provision.rs      @bradpenney

# --- supply chain -----------------------------------------------------------
# Pinned versions AND checksums. Changing a sha256 here changes which bytes run
# on every node and hypervisor.
/versions.yml                   @bradpenney
# CI has write access to this repository and publishes signed artifacts.
/.github/                       @bradpenney

# --- what the cluster trusts ------------------------------------------------
# Renders the cosign identity the cluster verifies against, the node SSH key,
# and the k0s API server flags.
/crates/substrate-core/src/render.rs         @bradpenney
/crates/substrate-core/src/config.rs         @bradpenney
/site.example.yml               @bradpenney
